meta {
  name: Get health
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq ok
  res.body.name: eq api
}

docs {
  The liveness verdict, from `RootUseCase` via `HealthController.root()`:

  ```json
  { "status": "ok", "name": "api" }
  ```

  Verdict only — it probes no database, queue or downstream service, so `ok` means this
  process is up and routing works and says nothing about anything behind it. `status` is
  the `ApiStatus` enum (`ok` | `error` | `pending`), which is why the assertion pins the
  value rather than only checking the field is there.

  `name` is what distinguishes this from the queue-coordinator's identical route, so a
  `baseUrl` pointing at the wrong service fails here instead of passing silently.
}
